## What Gets Created Automatically

**Important:** When using the `budi-kit new` command, ALL files are created automatically:

### Configuration Files (Static Templates)
- `package.json` - Package configuration and dependencies
- `.gitignore` - Git ignore patterns
- `.npmrc` - pnpm configuration
- `.prettierrc.json` / `.prettierignore` - Code formatting
- `.env.example` - Environment variable template
- `eslint.config.mjs` - Linting rules
- `next.config.ts` - Next.js configuration
- `tsconfig.json` - TypeScript configuration
- `.husky/pre-commit` / `.husky/pre-push` - Git hooks

### Application Files (Static Templates with Variable Substitution)
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Root layout with metadata
- `src/app/page.tsx` - Home page ("Hello World")
- `src/app/not-found.tsx` - 404 error page
- `src/app/loading.tsx` - Loading state component
- `src/app/robots.ts` - SEO robots configuration
- `src/lib/registry.tsx` - Styled-components SSR registry
- `src/styles/main.css` - Global styles and design system
- `src/types/index.ts` / `src/types/common.ts` - TypeScript types
- `src/components/index.ts` - Components barrel export

### Optional Components (Copied if Selected)
- Todo system files (`/dev/todo` route)
- Sanity CMS files (`sanity.config.ts`, `/admin/studio`)
- Cursor rules (`.cursor/rules/*.mdc`)

**No manual file creation is required.** The sections below serve as reference documentation.

